From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 06:07:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 18/57] fix: sprite bokeh sizes from the gather CoC and fades
 in step with the halo

The splat recomputed its circle of confusion from full-res depth while the gather blurred with its own 2x2-min / tile-dilated CoC, and an energy-conserving splat only gets brighter per pixel as a highlight nears focus while the gather's CoC-weighted halo fades - so a small sharp silhouette floated on an already-converged light, then vanished in one frame at the sub-pixel cull. The splat now reads the gather's CoC texture (SceneCoC[1]) and fades in over [1/3, 1] x r_DepthOfFieldSpriteBokehFadeCoC (new cvar, default 1.0). User-verified: focus pulls now read correctly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017nykaDjTHxHDSo11CsYx6M
